;; The config (session CONFIG, owner 2026-10-21: "the only things that should stay are documented
;; config schemas that we are porting from seon if they are relevant"). Each key's schema, in seon.config.<area>.edn,
;; states its default (:default) with its unit, provenance and what happens at its bound (owner, 2026-11-16: config
;; defaults live in the schema; malli's default-value-transformer applies them); resources/seon/config/default.edn states only what a schema
;; can't (values read from the process, #profile choices, #ref and #join paths). Each keeps v1's shape (~/src/seon resources/seon/schemas/
;; seon.config.*.edn): a schema with a :description and its :seon.config/unit.
;;
;; :seon.config/config is the whole resolved config, as malli reads it: open (owner, 2026-11-16: no closed map), so an unknown key is
;; carried and read by nothing; every entry required but those marked {:optional true} (a key its readers take as absent); a
;; required key's :default fills it before the check (malli.transform/default-value-transformer, seon.config/resolved), so a
;; key with a default is never missing and one with none must be given; that each has a value is
;; seon.config-test/the-shipped-file-validates-under-every-profile's,
;; and its entries declare the attributes root writes on the config entity on main (seon.task/config-tx).
